{
  "description": "Generic 2-tier (single-job) analytics dashboard for apps with no backend database: app + host only, no Layer 4/Database row. See 2-tier-fullstack-analytics for the full app+host+db dashboard.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [
    {
      "asDropdown": false,
      "icon": "arrow-left",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "tags": [],
      "targetBlank": false,
      "title": "← All Teams",
      "tooltip": "Back to the All Teams overview (this dashboard is shared across every team, so there's no single 'correct' team to return to)",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/all-teams-overview"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "title": "🟣  Layer 1 — The Four Golden Signals",
      "type": "row",
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Performance Drilldown →",
              "url": "/d/2-tier-no-db-analytics?var-job=$job&viewPanel=200",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "p99"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(app:http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(app:http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(app:http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Request Latency — p50 / p95 / p99",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "**What it measures:** Time from when the service receives a request to when it sends the response, expressed as percentile distributions.\n\n**p50 (median):** Half of requests complete faster than this. Represents the typical user experience.\n\n**p95:** 1 in 20 requests is slower than this. A good SLA target for most APIs.\n\n**p99:** 1 in 100 requests is slower than this. Reveals tail latency that averages hide — the experience of your worst-affected users.\n\n**How collected:** Prometheus Histogram metric (`http_request_duration_seconds`). The application records the duration of every request. PromQL `histogram_quantile()` computes percentiles from the bucket counts.\n\n**Thresholds:** Warn p99 > 1s · Critical p99 > 3s. Tighten for payment or auth flows (Warn > 500ms).\n\n**Common causes of spikes:** Slow database queries, GC pauses, downstream dependency latency, thread pool saturation.",
      "interval": "1m"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqpm",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Performance Drilldown →",
              "url": "/d/2-tier-no-db-analytics?var-job=$job&viewPanel=200",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 11,
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(app:http_requests_total{job=\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "Total RPS"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(app:http_requests_total{job=\"$job\",status_code=~\"2..\"}[$__rate_interval]))) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "2xx RPS"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Traffic — Requests per Minute",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "**What it measures:** The volume of requests your application is processing per second, broken down by HTTP status class.\n\n**Why it matters:** Traffic is your baseline. All other metrics must be interpreted relative to it. A 1% error rate means very different things at 10 RPS vs 10,000 RPS.\n\n**How collected:** Prometheus Counter (`app:http_requests_total`) incremented on every request. PromQL `rate()` converts the cumulative counter into a per-second rate over a sliding window.\n\n**What to watch:** Sudden drops (traffic fell away — routing issue?) are as important as spikes. Compare to same time yesterday using `offset 1d` in PromQL.\n\n**Thresholds:** Alert on deviation > 3× from rolling baseline rather than a fixed number.",
      "interval": "1m"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 15
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Error Drilldown →",
              "url": "/d/2-tier-no-db-analytics?var-job=$job&viewPanel=201",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "id": 12,
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(app:http_requests_total{job=\"$job\", status_code=~\"5..\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "5xx errors (count)"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(app:http_requests_total{job=\"$job\", status_code=~\"4..\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "4xx errors (count)"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Error Count — 4xx / 5xx (per scrape interval)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "**What it measures:** Number of error responses in each scrape interval.\n\nUses `increase()` over `$__rate_interval` so every data point shows the actual count of errors in that window — not a per-second rate.\n\n**Click any data point to open the Error Drilldown table** (per-endpoint breakdown).",
      "interval": "1m"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      },
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Saturation — CPU / Memory",
      "description": "**Resource saturation for the two most common host bottlenecks.** Normalised to 0-100%.\n\n- **CPU:** Average CPU utilisation across all cores on the host (from `node_exporter`).\n- **Memory:** Used RAM as a % of total (`MemAvailable` method, includes reclaimable cache).\n\n**Thresholds (shared):** Warn > 70% · Critical > 90%.",
      "type": "bargauge",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.7
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 80
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "valueMode": "color",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 13,
          "valueSize": 18
        },
        "minVizWidth": 0,
        "minVizHeight": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(100 - avg(rate(host:cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\", job=\"$host_job\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 100) / 100",
          "legendFormat": "CPU",
          "refId": "B",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "1 - (host:memory_available_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"} / host:memory_total_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"})",
          "legendFormat": "Memory",
          "refId": "C",
          "instant": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "id": 2,
      "title": "🟢  Layer 2 — Infrastructure & Host",
      "type": "row",
      "panels": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "percent",
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 10
              },
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "green",
                    "value": null
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "yellow",
                    "value": 70
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "red",
                    "value": 90
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 8,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 34
          },
          "id": 20,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "100 - (avg by(instance) (rate(host:cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\", job=\"$host_job\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 100)",
              "legendFormat": "{{instance}} CPU %"
            }
          ],
          "title": "CPU Utilization %",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** Percentage of CPU time spent on non-idle work per host, broken down by mode: user (application code), system (kernel), iowait (waiting for disk I/O), steal (stolen by hypervisor on VMs).\n\n**How collected:** `node_exporter` reads `/proc/stat` and exposes `host:cpu_seconds_total` counters per mode per core. PromQL computes the rate of non-idle time.\n\n**Thresholds:** Warn > 70% · Critical > 90% sustained for 5 minutes.\n\n**Key modes to watch:** High `iowait` means disk is the bottleneck. High `steal` means the VM host is overloaded — consider migrating to a less noisy host.",
          "interval": "1m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "bytes",
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 10
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 8,
            "x": 8,
            "y": 42
          },
          "id": 21,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "host:memory_total_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"} - host:memory_available_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"}",
              "legendFormat": "Used"
            },
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "host:memory_available_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"}",
              "legendFormat": "Available"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Memory — Used vs Available",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** RAM used by applications and the kernel vs RAM available for new allocations. Uses `MemAvailable` (not `MemFree`) which includes reclaimable page cache.\n\n**How collected:** `node_exporter` reads `/proc/meminfo` and exposes `node_memory_*` gauges.\n\n**Why MemAvailable matters:** Linux aggressively uses free RAM for file caching (beneficial). `MemFree` appears low even on healthy systems. `MemAvailable` is what the kernel can actually give to a new process.\n\n**Thresholds:** Warn when MemAvailable < 20% of total · Critical < 10%.\n\n**Watch for:** Any swap usage is a critical signal — apps hitting swap experience 100–1000× memory access latency.",
          "interval": "1m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "bytes",
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 10
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 8,
            "x": 16,
            "y": 50
          },
          "id": 22,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "host:memory_swap_total_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"} - host:memory_swap_free_bytes{job=\"$host_job\"}",
              "legendFormat": "Swap used"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Swap Usage (should be 0)",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** Amount of swap space (disk used as overflow memory) currently in use. Should always be zero on a healthy system.\n\n**Why it matters:** When a system uses swap, it is treating disk as RAM. Disk is 100–1000× slower than RAM. Any process reading from swap will experience severe latency spikes.\n\n**How collected:** `node_exporter` exposes `host:memory_swap_total_bytes` and `host:memory_swap_free_bytes`. Used = Total − Free.\n\n**Thresholds:** Any nonzero value is Critical — treat as a P1 incident. The OOM killer is the alternative, which terminates processes.\n\n**Common causes:** Memory leak, under-provisioned host, JVM heap set too large relative to available RAM.",
          "interval": "1m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "Bps",
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 8
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 8,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 58
          },
          "id": 23,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "rate(host:disk_read_bytes_total{job=\"$host_job\"}[$__rate_interval])",
              "legendFormat": "{{device}} read"
            },
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "rate(host:disk_written_bytes_total{job=\"$host_job\"}[$__rate_interval])",
              "legendFormat": "{{device}} write"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Disk I/O Throughput",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** Bytes read from and written to disk per second per device.\n\n**How collected:** `node_exporter` reads `/proc/diskstats` and exposes `host:disk_read_bytes_total` and `host:disk_written_bytes_total` counters.\n\n**Saturation metric:** `rate(node_disk_io_time_seconds_total[5m])` approaching 1.0 means the disk is 100% busy and I/O operations are queuing.\n\n**Thresholds:** Disk utilisation Warn > 70% · Critical > 90%. Write latency Warn > 10ms (SSD) · Warn > 50ms (spinning disk).\n\n**Common causes of high write I/O:** Database writes, application logging, backup jobs, log rotation.",
          "interval": "1m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "percentunit",
              "color": {
                "mode": "thresholds"
              },
              "min": 0,
              "max": 1,
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "green",
                    "value": null
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "yellow",
                    "value": 0.75
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "red",
                    "value": 0.9
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 8,
            "x": 8,
            "y": 66
          },
          "id": 24,
          "options": {
            "reduceOptions": {
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull"
              ]
            },
            "orientation": "auto"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "1 - (host:filesystem_avail_bytes{fstype!~\"tmpfs|overlay\", job=\"$host_job\"} / host:filesystem_size_bytes{fstype!~\"tmpfs|overlay\", job=\"$host_job\"})",
              "legendFormat": "{{mountpoint}}"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Disk Space Used %",
          "type": "gauge",
          "description": "**What it measures:** Percentage of disk space used per filesystem mount point.\n\n**How collected:** `node_exporter` reads filesystem stats via `statfs()` and exposes `host:filesystem_avail_bytes` and `host:filesystem_size_bytes`.\n\n**Thresholds:** Warn < 20% free · Critical < 10% free.\n\n**Best practice:** Alert on rate of fill, not just current percentage. A disk filling at 1GB/hour needs a different response than one filling at 1MB/hour. Use `predict_linear(host:filesystem_avail_bytes[6h], 4*3600) < 0` to alert when a disk will fill within 4 hours."
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "Bps",
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 8
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 8,
            "x": 16,
            "y": 74
          },
          "id": 25,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "rate(host:network_receive_bytes_total{device!~\"lo\", job=\"$host_job\"}[$__rate_interval])",
              "legendFormat": "{{device}} rx"
            },
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "rate(host:network_transmit_bytes_total{device!~\"lo\", job=\"$host_job\"}[$__rate_interval])",
              "legendFormat": "{{device}} tx"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Network Throughput RX / TX",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** Bytes received (RX) and transmitted (TX) per network interface per second.\n\n**How collected:** `node_exporter` reads `/proc/net/dev` and exposes `host:network_receive_bytes_total` and `host:network_transmit_bytes_total` counters per interface.\n\n**Thresholds:** Compare against your interface speed (1Gbps = 125MB/s). Alert when sustained throughput > 80% of interface capacity.\n\n**Also monitor:** `node_network_receive_drop_total` and `node_network_transmit_drop_total` — any packet drops indicate saturation or hardware issues.",
          "interval": "1m"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 82
      },
      "id": 3,
      "title": "🟡  Layer 3 — Application Layer",
      "type": "row",
      "panels": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "reqpm",
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 8
              }
            }
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 83
          },
          "id": 30,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "(sum by(route) (rate(app:http_requests_total{job=\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))) * 60",
              "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Request Rate by Endpoint (RPM)",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** HTTP requests per second broken down by individual route/endpoint.\n\n**Why it matters:** Aggregate traffic hides the distribution. 1,000 RPS could mean 990 on `/health` and 10 on `/checkout` — very different implications for scaling.\n\n**How collected:** `app:http_requests_total` counter with a `route` label set to the route template (e.g. `/api/orders/{id}` not `/api/orders/12345`). PromQL `sum by(route)` groups by endpoint.\n\n**Drill-down:** Click a spike on this chart to correlate with the latency panel — filter by the same route label to see whether the high-traffic endpoint is also slow.\n\n**Warning:** Never use user IDs or raw URLs as label values — this creates unbounded label cardinality that will crash Prometheus.",
          "interval": "1m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 12
              },
              "unit": "short",
              "links": [
                {
                  "title": "Error Endpoint Drilldown →",
                  "url": "/d/2-tier-no-db-analytics?var-job=$job&viewPanel=201",
                  "targetBlank": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 12,
            "y": 91
          },
          "id": 31,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
